bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/alignment-architecture.mem:63:The wiki does not hold a second HUD. The wiki holds ''the primitives that compose it'' — the sigil definitions, the `Aperture` / `OODA-HA` gauges, the glyph set, the HUD pair (`api/lares/hud` law + `docs/lares/hud` teaching), the memetic-wikitext grammar itself — each addressable by `lar:` and ''summonable into chat''. The session summons those primitives (by address, by `kahea`, by the grammar) and assembles them into the live HUD. The quine closes outward: the wiki //describes// the HUD in its own primitives, and the chat //summons that description to become// the HUD. The instrument self-hosts — ''defined in the wiki, run in chat''.
