bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/scale-stories-basket-one.mem:176:''The tension.'' A joinee that joins a PersonaGroup AFTER founding mints its wiki binding on its own vessel key — `"face-reach": seated ? "face" : "vessel-only"` (`packages/lararium-keyhive/src/resolve-binding.ts:156`) — and keeps it forever; a later `runFaceJoin` (`packages/lararium-keyhive/src/face-join.ts:197`) re-grants `daemonAuth.registerBags` and never re-delegates those earlier bindings (`packages/lararium-keyhive/src/face-join.ts`). The joinee-side gap reads wider: "no CLI verb, no daemon verb and no doc-relay path lands a later face-join grant ON THE JOINEE — the grant returns to the founder's caller" (`packages/lararium-keyhive/src/face-join.ts`). The door has two shapes: a daemon verb the founder's caller invokes on the joinee, or a doc the joinee watches for grants (`packages/lararium-keyhive/src/face-grant-record.ts` holds the door that got built). Beneath both sits the membership doctrine: "the face carries the credential, the group holds no list, and verification runs OFFLINE against a published key" (`bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine.mem:122`).
