bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae.mem:213:''The dyad binds at three doors, and each reads the fleet's own board.'' The root's admit door signs no delegation for a device its board shows set aside, so a fresh admit and a lease roll both skip that dyad. The Binding Gate refuses a boot whose own device edge stands shadowed, and the operator's own door names the reading. The join gate answers a summons from such a device with the words an edge that fails its signature draws, and names no cause. The face-grant seat and the sibling lane read the same shadow: a device set aside holds no seat there, whatever record or session it proves.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae.mem:246:''A device that returns takes its seat by its own fresh summons.'' The join re-keys each of the group's bags forward and re-seals nothing the group sealed before that seat, since those chunks hold the span the device missed. A holder hands that span over by a separate, explicit act alone. ''An earlier seat leaves first.'' Where a raise still owes its roll and the device still holds the seat that raise names, the join revokes that seat and then seats the device afresh; where its hand holds no authority over that seat, the join refuses, and the vessel that seated the device answers the raise first. A vessel that reads the raise and its lift together revokes the earlier seat and seats the device afresh in the same pass.
