bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/prism.mem:32:The node summons it. It never rides a turn by default.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:36:| Verb summonses and their answers | ''the face's intent plane'' (#/the-plane) | the channel of intent: addressed, answered by receipt, face-owned, clockless |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:47:* ''A fifth face plane'', `@intents-<tag>`, beside `@persona`, `@circles`, `@identities` and `@sessions` (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/automerge-tiga">>). It derives from the PersonaGroup's tag like its siblings, so every device that joins the face derives its name and syncs it with no extra provisioning; two faces on one device share no entry; nothing stands above it. The PersonaGroup mints it and delegates append to each device edge; the mint order binds as for every face plane.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:149:Row `I1` at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road">> carries the build, red-first in this order: the plane and its entry kinds; stand-down and the verb classes; the read-side winner; claims, takeover and causal voids; the face-join summons moving off the daemon doc onto the plane (closing "two hearths of one face"); the daemon wiki's view pane; the rubric's witness; then the far agent's relay seat after its own research. The CLI's per-invocation face naming (the session model's commit 5) lands beside the summons move, since an intent names its issuing face.
