bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane.mem:23:Order (controller, 2026-10-22): Wave D runs BEFORE K17-R. Circles and identities now travel to every device of a face, which raises the stakes of the omnibus node key.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane.mem:40:# ''The seat lands when the grant arrives'': one serialized seat act owns the later grant's take, verify, ingest and the floor lift, with one in-flight promise, so duplicate wakes coalesce and a wake that lands mid-act earns one trailing pass. Three causal wakes feed it and nothing else: a change on the retained PersonaGroup document, filtered to this vessel's `face-join-grant/v1` title; a daemon-layer change under the group's lease prefix, and, only while a grant waits unjudged on an unavailable lease frontier, any daemon-layer change (a late layer wakes it even when it holds no lease slot, since the composite forwards a joining layer's records as changes); and one replay at boot once the lease listener attaches. The PersonaGroup document listener attaches when that plane arrives and replays the act once, so a boot never waits on an unsynced plane and no grant falls between the boot pass and the listener. A signature reads judged only after its ingest lands (a definitive verify refusal judges once per boot); an ingest fault, or a lease frontier that reads unavailable, leaves the record unjudged for the next causal change. No clock, no poll, no retry timer. `faceSeated` reports `knowsAgent` and takes nothing; vessel-only reuse reads the record and returns it; the mint path waits for the seat act before it reads the seat. The binding rests in D, in the face subtree, never in the floor index. Reds: a grant arriving after a vessel-only binding seats and lifts with no binding call (control: no grant, the floor stays); a grant before the daemon layer stays unjudged until the layer's join seats it; duplicate pulses ingest once; an ingest fault then a later change still seats; a crash between ingest and lift finishes once at restart.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:195:* ''The system wikis release; every other wiki reads the floor'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-16). Only each Nexus's Kahu cabal writes the `lares` and `lararium` wikis and bags live. Every other wiki, and every other hand, mounts them read-only by CID: the latest release that cabal approved. The release rides the Nexus's crossroads board as its public answer, naming the floor CID under the Kahu steward's seal. The cabal approves the exact bytes under its charter's threshold, and a herm carries the answer without signing it. Every wiki mounts that floor through `@oracle`, which never writes. A vessel moves its floor pin only when it accepts a newer signed release. With no Nexus speaking, it stands on its last accepted floor, or on genesis. A face's wikis follow the floor of the Nexus that face stands in, so one vessel may hold two floors and never ties its faces together. An edit aimed at the floor copies up into the wiki's own working layer, and an offering back travels as a draft into the cabal's realm. A lone hearth is a Nexus of one, so its operator stands as its own Kahu. Row `W26` carries the build.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:203:* ''One Keyhive identity per PersonaGroup, none above them'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18: //"it's the only way to retain control over faces that don't know about each other"//). Each face's PersonaGroup owns its Keyhive identity, its event store, its registry, its archive and its content-key seat; no vessel-wide identity registers a face's bags, delegates them, or holds a face's group. Two faces of one vessel then never link on the wire, a removal from one face rolls that face's bags alone, and a bundle restores one face and nothing of another. Today the vessel's own identity registers every bag and delegates each face's bags through itself, and the vessel and every face share one event store and one content-key holder (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/keyhive-per-persona-group-2026">>). House readings under the operator's confidence, each naming what flips it: a herm keeps a floor-only transport key, behind a red test that it can neither author, resolve nor observe a face's capabilities, and holds no Keyhive identity if that test fails; several face hives share one process only after a substrate probe reads them isolated, and each face's hive runs in its own worker otherwise; co-mingled history migrates by fresh identities and an old mixed archive refuses by name, with no bridge; a founder that cannot leave its group leaves by a fresh PersonaGroup. Row `K15` carries the build, folding `W25` and `K12`; `W26`'s slice 3 waits on its face context.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:214:* ''One owner per registry; the floor reads by CID'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18: //"Architecture stands, leans stand"//). The `@oracle` document as a registry every vessel writes retires: one id carried one `lares` and one `lararium` pointer for the whole fleet, and a joined vessel's pointer replaced its hearth's, a shape a two-vessel probe and three shard runs measured. `@oracle` stands as the floor's read-face over a manifest CID, which a wiki mounts read-only by the pin its face accepted. Each registry carries only what its scope's owner writes: a vessel's bootstrap holds its own document pointers and its accepted floor pins; `@catalog` the operator's documents; the Kahu realm the live `lares` and `lararium` documents and their drafts; the crossroads board the Nexus's one public answer. The leans the ruling adopts: the Kahu realm holds the live system documents, with `bags/` projected on the Kahu's vessel alone; a one-seat founding lands a counted 1-of-1 Kahu-cabal admission for persona zero's group, so one predicate decides every hand's reach into system canon; the release answer, the Nexus's one public answer, names the Nexus AID, the charter epoch, the release before it and the floor manifest CID, sealed by the steward, with the promotion approval over the manifest's exact bytes riding attached; a vessel records an accepted release as a sealed hot row per (face, Nexus) that only a person's act moves; genesis bakes the first floor, a corpus CID in the seed. A signing domain of its own carries the release, `floor-release`, so no seal over another shape verifies as one (operator-approved, 2026-10-18). The shape and its slices stand at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane">>; rows `W26`, `W21` and `P8` carry the build.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:241:* ''The contract seam'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). N2, N4 and N5 stand handed back. Train W owns the admit-carriage hunk of `nexus-contract.ts` for the cutover, keeps N's anchor and prior-roll checks, and lands the contract, `device-admit.ts`, fleet answer, verifier and vectors as one signed-shape change. The reason: one signature shape must cross every producer and reader together. The ruling flips on a proven independent carriage boundary that preserves those checks and signed bytes.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:251:* ''Sync carries; verification decides'' (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the research at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/identity-invariants-2026">> and the controller's leans). A mutable CRDT carries identity claims and never decides them. Each face holds, on each device, a ''sealed identity anchor'' in its own custody (a D row): its PersonaGroup, its persona-KEL prefix, a commitment to its root, its device edge's digest, and a known frontier that never falls. Only founding, admission and the recovery rites (guardian rotation, bundle restore, root cards) write an anchor; sync never writes one. Founding and admission acts, device edges and lease advances travel as signed records in the face's `@persona` plane, a signed-entry log every reader verifies against the anchor and the KEL; two signed acts at one sequence surface as a fork, never a CRDT winner. The face planes hold verified projections. A device reads freely; an act that widens authority (admit, grant, re-key, seal to a reader) checks the sealed frontier and refuses a target that names a newer bound, its receipt naming the frontier it acted under. Transparency and witnesses for equivocation wait for their own row. Wave C carries the build inside `K15` step 6.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:254:* ''The order of the next waves'' (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the controller's leans). Wave C (`K15` step 6 under the identity anchor) runs next, with `W26`'s slices 3, 4 and 6 beside it on the floor's own ground, their composer hunks passing to the controller as patches, and slice 5 after it, since its accepted floor rests as a face's sealed row (a D row under the face's own FCK once Wave C lands); `I1` follows the anchor; the far agent's relay seat takes its own research after `I1`; `G37`'s renames ride `X0`'s bake; the sensorium resumes after `X0`, on the operator's word.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:256:* ''The edge frontier'' (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the controller's leans after the research at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/edge-frontier-2026">>). Nothing signed today lets a reader tell a device never set aside from a raise erased or withheld, so the house adds a signed ''edge frontier'' per board, its own domain-separated certificate type, the persona KEL resolving its signer's key. Every hand that can raise on a board signs its own stream's frontier (a fleet board's root; a realm board's charter quorum, with its holder where vouch edges raise), and a frontier commits its counted acts through its boundary as a content-addressed snapshot, its parent frontier, and its roster and epoch lineage. A raise shadows its target at once for every reader that sees it, and counts toward widening once its signer registers it into the next frontier. Sync always carries acts, frontiers and snapshots. A widening act (admit, grant, a content key sealed or re-sealed to a reader) reads its target against a frontier of every raising hand that extends any head the reader pinned and includes every raise it has seen; it acts as of that frontier, its receipt naming it, and waits as unknown where none qualifies. Every fleet and realm founds with a signed empty genesis frontier, and an admit bundle carries the current frontier and its snapshot. Until the row stands built, absence reads clear for sync and for widening alike, the gap named. Row `K17`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:287:* ''A long-silent fleet device'' catches up before it acts: a presentation carries its presenter's frontier of the face's withdrawal history, and a gate that holds a later one answers `unconfirmed` and hands over what the device lacks. No clock; a house reading the operator may overturn (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-withdrawal-proof">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:451:* ''Integrity owed: identity authority enforced, beyond the prose'' (`K15` step 6). Its witness: Wave C's red suite, a forged selector and a coherent foreign bundle refused, one sequence signed twice surfacing as a fork, a frontier that never falls. LEAD on the suite's shape; MEASURED that today's gate verifies continuity alone (`boot-daemon-keyhive.ts`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:459:* `K15` One hive per face (#/rulings, 2026-10-18): each PersonaGroup owns its Keyhive identity, event store, registry, archive and content-key seat, and no identity stands above them. Build order, each step red-first: (0) before bytes move, the custody contract of <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero">>: the node and browser row census sorted D, F or S, the FCK key class, each face's own slot tree and recovery route, the carrier binding of face, row name and kind, and the overwrite contract generalized to a row-class key (#/rulings, a face's custody rows seal under its own key; a shared act never makes a shared secret) (the node census built, PR #70: each carrier row names its target classes, a LEAD mark and its open joint, and `encodeCarrierContext` spells the D and S seal context; the archive-row-selector joint traced and held open, PR #71: no archive site hands its row an authenticated PersonaGroup); (1) a substrate probe that two Keyhive instances in one process hold apart under interleaved acts, a reboot and a cross-read (measured: isolation holds, `packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/two-hives-one-process.probe.test.ts`), then a face context with its own store, registry, archive and key seat; (2) the face as the sole owner of its identity and group, the vessel's delegation gone from every face-bearing event (built, PR #68: `makeFaceBagDoor`, `faceOwnerVerifier`, a two-face event-byte capture its red, `W25`'s probe its regression), and 2b, a bag keeping one Document across boots (built, PR #68: `registerBagsDurably`, its record on the daemon doc for the vessel's ground and on each face's plane for that face's bags); the door grants the face's group before it records a Document (PR #69), so a crash between them re-enters to the same end; (2c, operator ruling 2026-10-19; built, PR #79) the atom cut: a random atom per (vessel, PersonaGroup) under that face's FCK signs every act on the face's behalf on node and browser, the place signer keeps the floor's duties alone, the wire subjects and verifiers move together, and its genesis, admit and founding-bootstrap deltas ride `X0` by `genesis/unbaked.json`, red-first on a thief holding the place seed deriving no veil and opening no group secret; on the local presence channel the session wears the mounted face, so a verb's presenter derives from the island's own atom and never from the CLI's unsigned `requestedBy`, the floor presents the place for floor acts alone, and a verb that names another face refuses by name (#/rulings, a session wears the face, 2026-10-11; a published atom key would link face and vessel on a wire); (3) sessions and registries routed by one face, no union, with `F6` slice three's asker-seals beside it, each sealer holding its row class's key (built, PR #81: the browser house keys by (PersonaGroup, persona root), the island proves each face through `gate:clear` while the holder holds no key, the island reads the fleet board's dyad itself, a fresh group mints a fresh atom, founding seeds key by their ask digest, and the node keys its atom and veil-archive rows by PersonaGroup digest; the daemon's last unions ride step 6); (4) content keys and removal per face, `K12`'s fresh group inside it; (5) a one-face restore and a herm that carries yet authors nothing; (6) the fence migration, identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, and archive and custody formats together, under one identity model (#/rulings, sync carries, verification decides: the sealed anchor, the signed `@persona` log, verified projections): each D row (the atom's seed, its archive) seals under its face's FCK, where the node now seals them under the seated vessel key, and keys by its PersonaGroup, as the node's atom and veil-archive rows and the browser's atom row already do, where the browser's veil archive still keys by handle index. The isolation red: unlock face A alone, bypass every route, and try to open and replace B's occupied carriers with every key A holds, the S key included; each open fails, B's bytes stand unchanged, and A's bundle restored on a fresh vessel holds nothing of B. Lead: DreamNet-Wright after `W26`'s floor slice lands. K, W. Wave C (step 6 under the identity anchor, `readFace` as the one door with its census) landed in PR #86 on 2026-10-23. `K15-H` (the Handle owner rides the anchor, the row in `docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane`) landed in PR #88. Wave D (the FCK fence, its eight slices whole, kit `docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane`) landed in PR #95 on 2026-10-26: each face seals its D rows under its own FCK, unlocks apart, bundles and restores alone, lifts its anon veil on join, and seats when its grant arrives. `K17`'s realm leg (`docs/pono/k17-realm-lease-lane`) runs next.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:481:* `K17` The edge frontier (#/rulings, the edge frontier, 2026-10-20). Red-first: the frontier certificate and its verifier on node and browser alike; the signed empty genesis at every founding; registration of a raise into its signer's next frontier; the widening reader (admit, grant, a content-key seal) acting as of a qualifying frontier and waiting as unknown otherwise; the admit bundle carrying the frontier and its snapshot; the reader persisting its highest accepted head. Reds: a withheld first raise, a deleted local raise, a stale clean frontier, two conflicting frontiers, a missing snapshot, a concurrent raise and lower, an epoch rollover. Beside Wave C, on the spine. K.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:482:* `K18` The recovery door: guardian-quorum rotation of a persona root beneath its KEL prefix, then `reanchorAfterRotation`, then a re-admit carrying the current `@persona` log and signed frontier. Owed: no production door rotates a root today, and the ceremony waits on the guardian count, an open operator gate (`kahu#/seed-and-nexus`); `reanchorAfterRotation` stands proven as a library function (Wave C, <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane">> #/owed). K.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:506:* ''Integrity owed: the floor's trust chain'' (`W14`, `W15`, `W16`: the signed floor card, the pin's causal position, carry-floor convergence). Its witness: a rotation-and-carry storm that accepts no stale pin and converges the same way on every carrier.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:512:* `W14` The floor card a banner carries in its `#floor=` link reads unsigned, on origin trust; a signed card stays owed. The floor read by release (`W26` slice 4) adds one rung and closes nothing here: a browser holding the Nexus AID verifies the epoch lineage, the head release and the floor bytes itself (`browser-floor-read`), anchored to the AID alone, since the genesis epoch re-derives it. The lineage rides the release record and the porch answer, never the card (a card holds 4096 characters, and the lineage self-certifies); that carrier changes nothing about trust, because the AID that anchors it comes from the card or the genesis CID the reader already pins and never from the answer, and an answer self-consistent for another AID refuses (`floor-answer.test`). The AID itself still rides the same-origin trust line, and nothing proves the card's freshness: the signed card (`W14`), the pin's causal position (`W15`) and the carry-floor convergence (`W16`) stay owed for anchoring the AID and the card. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:513:* `W15` A floor pin statement carries no causal position, and `hearthPinIndex` files first-wins, so a rotated floor key re-files only on restart (`admit-gate-pin.ts`, `place-floor-pin.ts`). W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:514:* `W16` Two-vault carry: the carry partials land no floor pin, so a cofounded Nexus carries no herm yet (`nexus-contract.ts`). W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:515:* `W26` The system wikis release and every other wiki reads the floor (#/rulings, 2026-10-16). Slice 1 stands (PR #49): genesis carries the first floor, its manifest and the `lares` and `lararium` snapshots by CID, and `@oracle` reads that floor by CID. Slice 2 stands (PR #52): each vessel's system, crossroads and realm pointers rest in its own `@catalog`, and nothing writes the shared `@oracle` after genesis (`oracle-doc-no-writer.test.ts`). Slice 3 stands (lane `--w26-floor-3`): the founding lands the counted 1-of-1 Kahu admission for persona zero's group (`landFoundingAdmission`) and registers `lares` and `lararium` as realm bags of the hearth's realm under persona zero's per-Nexus key (`landKahuRealm`); `kahuCabalCanonAccess` has its production caller (`kahuReachSourceOf`); the keel mounts only what the realm names, the registered bag set and the `bags/` mirrors follow, and no catalog row names a system bag. Slice 6 stands: one predicate (`requireKahuReach`) guards the residency reactor, meme put and delete, draft placement and a realm steward's write, and the keyholder island's verifier carries it for `--in-wiki` verbs. Slice 4 stands: the release (`floor-release`: body, CID, steward seal by a seated Kahu key, the cabal's high-impact approval of the manifest's exact bytes, the charter's epoch lineage), the chain fold, `lares nexus release`, the porch (`GET /floor/<Nexus AID>`, `/cas/<cid>` for the head's blobs), the browser's verified read, and the flow map's own `flow-pointer` domain in place of the retired `oracle-pointer`. The build runs six slices in order, under the architecture of #/rulings (2026-10-18), its shape and evidence at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane">>: (1) the floor manifest and its read-face, genesis baking the first floor; (2) each vessel's pointers leave the shared document for its bootstrap, re-cutting `W21`; (3) the Kahu realm holds the live system documents, and a one-seat founding lands its 1-of-1 Kahu admission; (4) the release answer on the crossroads, folding `P8`; (5) the accept act per (face, Nexus), which follows Wave C's face context since its accepted floor rests as a face's D row; (6) reach into system canon refuses every hand outside the cabal. OWED: a browser Kahu hand rides Wave C's face context (the browser composes no board reader and reads as a stranger, fail closed); a sibling device of a seat-holding face reads the floor until that context carries the charter and the board to it; the carriage `canon` names (`device-admit.ts` `admitCanonDocs`, the browser's `hearth-canon`) read rows nothing writes now, and retire with `W21`'s rest. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:536:* ''Integrity owed: the bake's cross-product'' (`X0`, touching `K15` step 6, `W26`, `G37`). Its witness: one matrix over the pre-bake and post-bake artifacts, every old CID refused after the bake and a fresh two-of-two founding standing, rather than greens read row by row.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:543:* `G37` The evergreen sweep of 2026-10-18 (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/evergreen-sweep-2026">>, its six rulings and fourteen lanes). Built: (1) the standing witness `tools/evergreen-boundary.mjs` (PR #53), its ceilings version 59 (F6's envelope took five), clock 57 (the engine watch took two, the cap-event rows one) and narration 202 (W27 took one) over 1079 files; (8) the engine watch reads an engine by its sha256 (PR #60); (5) worldline replay orders by parent links and handle dependencies and names every skip (PR #62), the mempalace KG still dropping `parentKey` when it persists and the CLI tree's sequential mark still reading recorded times, each exception naming its rule, file, line, count and reason; (2) `bytesEqual`, `constantTimeBytesEqual`, a strict `hexToBytes` and `nexusAidOfPin` in `@lararium/mesh` (PR #51). Order of the rest: (3) opaque ids, the mount nonce, optional display times and parent-link worldline replay, after `W26` slice 2, the clock sinks at effect-record, residency-actions, sense-sensorium, handler-args, engine-watch, wiki-behavior, verb-tiddler and vessel-mailbox; (4) the engine watch by CID, the `LarDoc` and session-envelope shapes, the floor announcement's kind and the browser store's current shape; (5) the numbered preimages and formats renamed together in the bake that closes `W26`, the signing preimages outside `domains.ts` among them (holder-continuity, persistence-keel, wax-stamp's `lar-*/v1`), which take the same frozen-preimage ruling as `engine/v1`. Each lane red-first under a clock set to 1970 and to 3000. G.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:544:* `X0` The founding bake: one deliberate re-genesis before a second operator stands, after which CIDs are meant to last because another operator pins them. It moves together `K15` step 6 (identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, archive and custody formats, each face's random device veil), the place KEL's pre-rotation and the scoped place signer (the signer frames each duty's domain itself, signing `len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage` and its verifiers the same, so no signed floor image carries its own separation; until then each of the five floor duties binds its domain by an exact head matcher), `W26`'s closing bake (the floor release), and `G37`'s preimage and format renames (`engine/v1` and its kin, the floor announcement's kind, the genesis seed and CAS formats). Each member carries its own readiness red, so the bake waits on the slowest by name, never on a date; the bake's own red: a fresh genesis founds, no CID from before the bake verifies after it, and a mixed old archive refuses by name. The gate it opens: a second operator may found a Nexus fresh at two of two. X.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:579:* `P8` One public answer per Nexus, signed by the steward: the floor release answer, built as `W26`'s release slice (#/rulings, 2026-10-18): the body, the steward's seal, the approval and the porch stand (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu">> #/floor-release). The domain's Handle table stays here, off the ceremony's chain by ruling. P, W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:663:* `W21` A joinee mounts the hearth's `@lararium` corpus read-only beside its own, while the oracle plane never crosses (#/rulings, 2026-10-16). Each vessel's pointers rest in its own `@catalog` (PR #52), so a joined vessel's pointer no longer replaces its hearth's, and `shared-oracle-doc.probe` holds that two synced vessels each keep their own. The rest rides `W26`'s floor slices: a joinee reads its hearth's floor by the release and its CIDs (slice 4), where slice 5's accept act moves its pin; a sibling device of a seat-holding face reads the floor until Wave C's face context carries the charter and the board to it, and `device-admit.ts` states the law. W.
